Check the reasoning in this case. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {3, 7, 11, 15, 17, 20, 23, 28};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 3) return steps; if (a[mid] < 3) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps;

