int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i += 2) acc += a[i];
return acc;

Given this setup, find the answer. What does this string routine return?
String s = "aocycyda";
int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++)
  if ("aeiou".indexOf(s.charAt(i)) >= 0) acc++;
return acc;

Trace the behavior described here. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {-2, 0, 1, 3, 7, 11, 15};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 1) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 1) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

Here is a problem to analyze. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(10);
Node b = new Node(15);
Node c = new Node(5);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

